            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="0834" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/15272.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Brazilian Minister to Mexico</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-22T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1915—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>795. Your 650, June 17, 6 p.m. Silliman telegraphs: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Previous assurances of guaranties by Gonzalez repeated. No responsibility
                            assumed for consequences of resistance by forces occupying city or for
                            disorder or depredations attending evacuation.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. Osborne.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
